      "end_summary": "Fixed the issue where the Kubernetes Python client doesn't honor the `tls-server-name` setting from kubeconfig.\n\n**Changes made to `kubernetes/base/config/kube_config.py`:**\n\n1. **`_load_cluster_info` method**: Added reading of `tls-server-name` from the cluster section of kubeconfig:\n   ```python\n   if 'tls-server-name' in self._cluster:\n       self.tls_server_name = self._cluster['tls-server-name']\n   ```\n\n2. **`_set_config` method**: Added propagation of `tls_server_name` to the Configuration object:\n   ```python\n   if hasattr(self, 'tls_server_name'):\n       client_configuration.tls_server_name = self.tls_server_name\n   ```\n\n**Result:** The `tls-server-name` value from kubeconfig is now properly propagated to the `Configuration` object as `tls_server_name`, which can be used by the API client for proper TLS SNI handling. All 78 tests in `kube_config_test.py` pass, including the `test_tls_server_name` test.",
